{"id": "EUVD-2026-71286", "enisaUuid": "75c1a020-976e-38dd-b7a3-803fb548cbe1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: virtio - bound the akcipher result length\n\nvirtio_crypto_dataq_akcipher_callback() sets the result length from the\ndevice-reported response length without bounding it to the destination\nbuffer, which was allocated for the original request length.\nsg_copy_from_buffer() then reads that many bytes from the destination\nbuffer; a backend reporting a larger length over-reads adjacent kernel\nheap into the caller's scatterlist (an out-of-bounds read).\n\nClamp the reported length to the originally requested destination length.\nA conforming device reports no more than that, so valid results are\nunaffected.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:54:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd33cb19bcb432a4dd5e8f50be5e2547af1e9f78", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/12c4f29e97f31b013f77ad65ba7daeb02aaa6abe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5545de5050cbc3594506d74f2c392b0716cf8bca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3fda114a42f1510a4ec8a0b17a0cfc997952ccc2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f9f877b1ef1fbd4ee95571cddf39c8002cee252", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f77a956f6a19f9463ef1527c9d0cda50dded6b92"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80836", "GHSA-4c27-p37x-4j2h"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f8753fc-187f-35aa-ba2f-4f2859b854ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36bd0ad9fbf69d0d711b1c105954ce8d6cc144a <3fda114a42f1510a4ec8a0b17a0cfc997952ccc2"}, {"id": "15bf8d15-1e25-34e8-9e05-c7c2ba245d23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36bd0ad9fbf69d0d711b1c105954ce8d6cc144a <1f9f877b1ef1fbd4ee95571cddf39c8002cee252"}, {"id": "2804daa1-d202-3464-aaf3-f4ec64db5551", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36bd0ad9fbf69d0d711b1c105954ce8d6cc144a <5545de5050cbc3594506d74f2c392b0716cf8bca"}, {"id": "5360b593-8ec7-3fb3-ae7f-7a49f83ed2c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5528ccc0-96cb-3727-9bbb-a3e2f5814709", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.49"}, {"id": "64b95ada-62d4-3345-972c-7f7ec7f7ae80", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36bd0ad9fbf69d0d711b1c105954ce8d6cc144a <bd33cb19bcb432a4dd5e8f50be5e2547af1e9f78"}, {"id": "7a524508-b728-348c-8ec5-1bd4f3a19253", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36bd0ad9fbf69d0d711b1c105954ce8d6cc144a <f77a956f6a19f9463ef1527c9d0cda50dded6b92"}, {"id": "8533fdf8-02f5-35c4-bd4b-323631250d57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36bd0ad9fbf69d0d711b1c105954ce8d6cc144a <12c4f29e97f31b013f77ad65ba7daeb02aaa6abe"}, {"id": "8e1d4973-5f52-3858-9d25-d16be9c9ac7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}, {"id": "983b94c8-51f0-361d-ad81-fd71577e2a49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "9a6b9e9a-6290-394f-91a1-b036ae285a5a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "b27a5e40-8ba9-364e-9d67-09977c8539f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ce0244ad-5c0d-3a7b-9ef0-8eebf67b56b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.13"}, {"id": "f72e1014-0df8-35da-a5ff-3a3b3e8f1e36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.19"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "34037798-62d6-31e1-b0a8-0b0cfdc77c9e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}